# Surface Department

- **Territory & Key Files** (planned — update paths as the scaffold lands)
  - `**/views/**`, `**/urls.py` — class-based views preferred; thin views that call Ledger services
  - `**/templates/**` — Django templates + HTMX; public Capability Record page is the flagship surface
  - `**/forms.py` — all incoming data validated through forms; no raw `request.POST` reads in views
  - `**/integrations/**` — Stripe Checkout/Portal, AI draft provider, S3 evidence storage; one module per provider

- **Idioms**
  - Client access is credentialled by email, never by account: a magic link establishes a session carrying a verified client email, and clients still have no `User`, `Profile`, password or handle. Project-scoped action links remain tokenized. Both the session check and the token check live in shared mixins, never in per-view copies
  - AI provider is draft-only: output lands in editable form fields with an explicit human-confirm step before any client-facing state change
  - Errors to users are friendly and generic; details go to server logs (minus PII/tokens per constitution)
  - Uploads enforce MIME/size limits at the form layer with friendly errors
  - HTMX partials live beside their page templates; no inline scripts that would weaken CSP

- **Hazards**
  - Ledger territory is read-only from here — views call services, never mutate trust objects directly (that includes `.status` writes)
  - Stripe webhook/redirect handlers and billing gates → full dispatch, gate applies
  - Public Capability Record rendering must respect dispute-freeze state — do not cache it into staleness
  - Magic-link token generation/validation is auth-flow code: changes require explicit plan authorization

- **Verification**
  - `.\.venv\Scripts\python manage.py test <app_label>` (scoped) then full suite
  - Smoke: request public record page + one tokenized client view; assert 200 and no PII/tokens in rendered output
